# Source preparation pipeline to be run from mapterhorn/pipelines folder.
# Real (non-trial) coverage for Otaru + Cape Kamui + Cape Shakotan
# (小樽市＋神威岬＋積丹岬) -- a coastal peninsula, chosen for terrain
# diversity (narrow capes jutting into the sea) distinct from Hakodate's
# broader peninsula and Sapporo's inland plain/single mountain. Scope
# approximation (no real administrative boundary available): lon
# 140.45-141.05, lat 43.15-43.45, spanning 1st-level mesh blocks
# 6440 (R5-7/C3-7), 6441 (R5-7/C0), 6540 (R0-1/C3-7), 6541 (R0-1/C0).
# Deliberately built now, ahead of this session's fresh Hokkaido
# DEM1A-20260616 convert+sync, using whatever is *currently* published
# on Source Cooperative -- the purpose of this run is to validate
# today's aggregation_run.py/aggregation_tile.py fixes (DECISIONS.md
# D12), not to produce final-quality coverage; expect a rebuild once
# the fresh Hokkaido data lands (see HANDOVER.md).
# 1,250 files after deduplicating same-position files published under
# multiple survey dates (257 stale-dated duplicates removed -- SC's
# additive-only sync had left older and newer versions of the same
# mesh coexisting; kept the newest date per position). jpsapporo1's
# file_list.txt predates this dedup logic and may have the same issue,
# unverified.
# source_to_cog.py deliberately skipped, same reasoning as jpsapporo1.
[no-cd]
default:
    uv run python source_download.py jpshakotan1
    uv run python source_bounds.py jpshakotan1
    uv run python source_polygonize.py jpshakotan1 4
